<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Schuman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1886–1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Schuman was a French Christian Democratic politician who served as prime minister and foreign minister under the Fourth Republic. On 9 May 1950 he proposed pooling French and German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> production, the Schuman Declaration, which led to the European Coal and Steel Community. He is regarded as one of the founders of European integration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-schuman.jpg" alt="Robert Schuman" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Commission · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Schuman_1958.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
